+## Disposition: ACCEPT as a rigorous, honest NO-GO (stop b)
+
+The Fourier / representation-theory route to an all-n minimax-depth lower bound
+beyond the information bound is cleanly closed as a method family. S(n) and
+SORT-BOUND-U remain OPEN. This is a legitimate barrier result (one of the
+productive frontiers named in AGENTS.md: "barriers that rule out whole families
+of methods"), not a theorem completion and not filler.
+
+### Ground 1 — universal cap (method-independent, verified)
+
+Sergeev's primary theorem `S(n) = log2(n!) + O(n/(log n)^(1/5))` is confirmed at
+`docs/research-sergeev-asymptotic.md:8` (ECCC TR20-096 Thm 3; journal DOI
+10.1134/S0965542521020111). Since any valid lower bound I satisfies
+`I(A_n) <= F(A_n) = S(n)`, its surplus over information obeys
+`I(A_n) - log2(n!) <= O(n/(log n)^(1/5)) = o(n)`. Therefore the front's positive
+bar — surplus `omega(n/polylog n)` beyond information at the antichain — is
+unsatisfiable for ANY technique: it would have to exceed the true value's own
+surplus. The front was mis-specified; its "empty gap" observation is correct.
+
+Referee note (not a correction): `omega(n/polylog n)` is ambiguous about the
+polylog exponent; under the weaker reading `n/(log n)^k, k<1/5` the universal
+cap alone would not close the bar. The no-go is nonetheless robust because
+Ground 2 is self-contained and holds under every reading.
+
+### Ground 2 — technique-specific root degeneracy (verified)
+
+At the antichain A_n, Ext(A_n) = S_n (all n! permutations are linear extensions),
+so the indicator `1_{Ext(A_n)}` is the constant 1 on S_n. Its representation-
+theoretic Fourier transform is supported only on the trivial irrep `(n)` and
+vanishes on every nontrivial irrep. Hence Plancherel weight on nontrivial
+irreps, the transposition-Cayley-graph spectral gap on subrepresentations, and
+Fourier concentration/uncertainty all evaluate to 0 or the trivial value at the
+root: the concrete route yields exactly `log2(n!)` at A_n (zero surplus). The
+random-transposition walk's `Theta(n log n)` mixing scale matches the
+information scale (Diaconis-Shahshahani), so it supplies no positive surplus.
+Sound and independent of Sergeev.
+
+### Ground 3 — honest blocker (verified against canonical doc)
+
+The only quantity provably equal to the surplus is the entropy-bias term
+`k - log2(n!) = E[k-D] + sum_v q_v(1-h2(p_v))`
+(`docs/research-sergeev-asymptotic.md:41`), a functional of the adaptive tree /
+adversary distribution, not a Fourier invariant of the state. A representation-
+theoretic formula for the conditional bias p_v at reachable states in terms of
+Fourier coefficients of `1_{Ext(P)}` would be needed; Ground 1 shows it cannot
+reach the front's stated bar. Correctly reported as a blocker, not a theorem.
+
